{
  "id": "Compound::DB01045 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Rifampicin exhibits a strong binding interaction with Cyp3a4, as evidenced by multiple paths showing its interaction with Cyp3a43 and Cyp3a7, both of which participate in aromatase activity. This suggests that Rifampicin may modulate the activity of Cyp3a4 through its interaction with these isoforms. The shared involvement of Cyp3a4 in aromatase activity implies that Rifampicin could influence the metabolism of steroid hormones, potentially affecting estrogen levels. The presence of multiple pathways linking Rifampicin to Cyp3a4 through different isoforms highlights the complexity of its interaction with the cytochrome P450 system. The evidence supports a mechanism where Rifampicin may inhibit Cyp3a4 activity, thereby altering the metabolism of xenobiotics and steroid hormones. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of Cyp3a4 in drug metabolism and its potential role in mediating Rifampicin's effects.",
